{
  "$comment": "Language-agnostic corpus of the `schema-mutation-payload-parity` lint (`🧬️schema/📋️orchestration/🟦️.ts`, region ⚖️MutationPayloadParity). Each case gives a Rust aggregate source, the variant, a leaf payload schema, an optional aggregate schema and a committed fixture value; an optional `leafRust` holds the leaf enum whose `#[mutation_leaf(payload = <Variant>)]` makes it a wrapped leaf (only that variant's content is editable and witnesses the leaf schema); it expects the wire layout read off `#[value(...)]`, the variant wire name, the leaf payload `payload_value()` yields (`null` when the fixture is not that variant in that layout) and the findings as sorted `class@pointer` strings; a given aggregate schema's branch is the one the repo-wide rule derives (`mutationAggregateBranch`). The third-party oracle (Ajv 2019 with `unevaluatedProperties: false`) must agree on every `invalid` and `undescribed` verdict. `features` pins the wire-form row reader `mutationFeatureRows` over the harness's own `parseFeature`: every expanded step docstring `{\"kind\": <k>, \"params\": <p>}` is a row at its scenario's line; data tables and other templates are not.",
