  "features": [
    {
      "id": "only-outline-rows-with-a-kind-and-params-template-are-wire-rows",
      "source": "Feature: Apply every typed mutation\n\n  @id-table\n  @level-quick\n  @mode-conformance\n  Scenario: A plain scenario keeps its data table out\n    Given the document\n      | kind | params |\n      | set-text | {\"path\": [9]} |\n\n  @id-mutate\n  @level-exhaustive\n  @mode-differential\n  Scenario Outline: Apply <id> to the real document\n    When the <id> mutation is applied with its parameters\n      \"\"\"\n      {\"kind\": \"<id>\", \"params\": <params>}\n      \"\"\"\n    Then the projection moved\n    Examples:\n      | id       | params                                   |\n      | set-text | {\"path\": [2], \"text\": \"World\"}            |\n      | set-name | {\"path\": [], \"name\": \"g\"}                |\n\n  @id-vector\n  @level-exhaustive\n  @mode-conformance\n  Scenario Outline: Vectors use another template and are skipped\n    When the <id> vector runs\n      \"\"\"\n      {\"kind\": \"<id>\", \"vector\": \"<vector>\"}\n      \"\"\"\n    Examples:\n      | id       | vector |\n      | set-text | v1     |\n",
      "rows": [
        {
          "line": 14,
          "kind": "set-text",
          "params": {
            "path": [
              2
            ],
            "text": "World"
          }
        },
        {
          "line": 14,
          "kind": "set-name",
          "params": {
            "path": [],
            "name": "g"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "only-when-steps-that-apply-the-named-kind-are-wire-rows",
      "source": "Feature: Only mutation steps are wire rows\n\n  @id-identity-round-trip\n  @level-long\n  @mode-round-trip\n  Scenario: Decode and re-encode the committed artifact\n    Given the plugin's own committed DSL artifact asset://demo\n    When it is parsed with parse_dsl and printed back with print_dsl\n    Then the printed bytes are identical to the committed bytes\n      \"\"\"\n      {\"kind\": \"identity-round-trip\", \"params\": {\"carrier\": \"byte-exact\"}}\n      \"\"\"\n\n  @id-inverse\n  @level-exhaustive\n  @mode-property\n  Scenario Outline: Undoing <id> restores the document\n    Given the committed before-snapshot\n    When the <id> mutation is applied and then undone with its own inverse\n      \"\"\"\n      {\"kind\": \"<id>\", \"params\": <params>}\n      \"\"\"\n    Then the projection equals the base projection again\n      \"\"\"\n      {\"kind\": \"<id>\", \"params\": <params>}\n      \"\"\"\n    Examples:\n      | id       | params                  |\n      | set-name | {\"path\": [], \"name\": \"g\"} |\n\n  @id-refused\n  @level-quick\n  @mode-error\n  Scenario: A refused kind is attempted\n    When the set-text mutation is attempted with its parameters\n      \"\"\"\n      {\"kind\": \"set-text\", \"params\": {\"path\": [7], \"text\": \"x\"}}\n      \"\"\"\n",
      "rows": [
        {
          "line": 17,
          "kind": "set-name",
          "params": {
            "path": [],
            "name": "g"
          }
        },
        {
          "line": 34,
          "kind": "set-text",
          "params": {
            "path": [
              7
            ],
            "text": "x"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
